"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The project has successfully completed its testing and design phases, with lead developer Omar Jensen guiding the upcoming development phase starting next month. A significant milestone was reached with the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, ahead of schedule, with user interface enhancements planned for October. The project budget was initially $500,000, adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration, and later approved at $2M by the executive board to cover all research, development, and marketing phases. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated effective January next year. The team has expanded with Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Additionally, partnership discussions are underway with TechInnovate for AI technology integration. A celebration for the testing phase milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
